# Twisted Roots Merc — what never goes in the repo (and therefore never ships)
#
# The repo root IS the published website. There is no build step and no dist/
# folder, so ANYTHING COMMITTED HERE IS DOWNLOADABLE BY THE PUBLIC at
# https://twistedrootsmerc.com/<that-path>. Treat this file as the deploy
# filter, not just a tidiness tool.
#
# Before adding something here, ARCHIVE IT (Drive/Dropbox) first. Ignoring a
# file does not delete it locally, but the repo stops being its backup.

# ─── dev artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
server.log
fetch*.log
*.log
nohup.out
contact*.png
slots*.json
fetch_stock.py
*.bak

# ─── source PNGs for generated art (the optimized .jpg ships instead) ───────
# ~45 MB of tr-*.png and ~36 MB of w-*.png masters, none of them referenced by
# any .html, .css or .js. ARCHIVE THE MASTERS before committing this file.
assets/img/tr-*.png
assets/img/w-*.png

# ─── page-assembly tooling (dev only — must NOT be published) ───────────────
# _parts/ holds the header/footer fragments build.py stitches into each page.
# Harmless EXCEPT _parts/hq.html, which is a copy of the PRIVATE owner
# dashboard markup. Published, it would sit at
#     https://twistedrootsmerc.com/_parts/hq.html
# completely outside whatever protection you put on /hq. This is not
# hypothetical — it is the exact file that would leak. Keep it out.
# Keep the folder on the owners' machine and in the shared drive.
# See DEPLOY.md → "Where the working files live".
/_parts/
/build.py
/build_blog.py
/_build_board.py

# blog/data/ is the SOURCE the blog builder reads. Note this ignores the
# source only, NOT blog/ itself — if build_blog.py starts emitting
# blog/*.html, those are real public pages and must ship. Add them to
# sitemap.xml when they appear.
/blog/data/

# ─── transactional email templates (not web pages) ──────────────────────────
# email/*.html are Gmail/Outlook templates for order and pickup mail. They are
# not part of the website and would otherwise be browsable at /email/. They
# belong with the sending platform's configuration, not the public site.
/email/

# ─── internal documents (would be world-readable if committed) ──────────────
# Keep these in a SEPARATE PRIVATE repo (suggested: twisted-roots-docs).
/TECH-PLAN.md
/QA-REPORT.md
/seo/
/print/
assets/css/MOTION-USAGE.md

# ─── OS and editor junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# ─── local tooling / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars


# ─── Deliberately NOT ignored (these must ship) ─────────────────────────────
#   index.html merc.html bakery.html yard.html storm.html
#   local.html roots.html visit.html hq.html
#   robots.txt sitemap.xml assets/
#   _headers _redirects   (Cloudflare Pages reads them and does not serve them)
#
# README.md and deploy/ DO ship and ARE publicly readable. Neither is secret,
# but README.md names hq.html. /_redirects already bounces /README.md to the
# home page. Add /deploy/ here once you have moved _headers and _redirects to
# the root, if you want it gone too.
